{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"},{"type":"text","text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle","anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"],"syntax":null},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generic "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store"},{"type":"text","text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A fifth method, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins","anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Core Middleware","anchor":"Core-Middleware"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" are "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"action-agnostic infrastructure"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":". They never inspect the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"type":"text","text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" needs keypaths to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" properties."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" needs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State: Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" so it can snapshot and compare."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Domain Plugins","anchor":"Domain-Plugins"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"domain-specific modules"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Comparison","anchor":"Comparison"},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Core Middleware","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain Plugins","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Action knowledge","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Lifecycle hooks","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns effects","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State coupling"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" constraint"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Wiring","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construction only"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Target","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":" library","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Separate library target","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Opt-in","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Instantiate and register","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add state, action case, and register","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Decision Rule","anchor":"The-Decision-Rule"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}]},{"text":", it’s core middleware — put it in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":" and use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":". If ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"yes","type":"text"}]},{"text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"important","name":"Important"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Hook Selection Guide","anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Capture state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Handle domain-specific actions ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Observe state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush() async"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Registration Order","anchor":"Registration-Order"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Next Steps","anchor":"Next-Steps"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware","type":"text"}]}]}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Explanation","title":"Explanation","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"]}],"metadata":{"title":"Plugin Architecture","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"observation layer."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","role":"symbol","title":"Store","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","title":"PluginHost","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","role":"symbol","title":"EntityStore","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"PersistencePlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Building a Domain Plugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","title":"UndoPlugin","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","title":"Architecture & Performance","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Design Principles"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Persistence Middleware"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","title":"SwiduxPlugin","type":"topic"}}}